        "_note": "Historical home for documented residuals between box-score figures and ESPN's official scores for the in-progress 2026 season. WEEKS 18-19 originally carried mixed-regime capture artifacts (backfilled snapshots vs live day-by-day) plus late MLB stat revisions landing after capture; active-slot sums drifted up to +/-112pt against official scores while player total_points mostly reconciled. RESOLVED 2026-08-25: extract.py gained --refresh-decided-weeks (wired into the heavy workflow step), which force-refetches every scoring period of fully-decided regular-season weeks on each heavy run, so per-period captures are always re-taken against ESPN's post-revision finals before normalize/validate reconcile them. The first healed run reconciled every documented gap to +/-0.0 and week 20 reconciled exactly on its first decided validation -- all weekly_shortfalls pins were removed. The pinning mechanism stays as the tripwire: validate.py warns (never fails) when a pinned gap heals to zero -- prompting pin removal like this one -- and fails only when a nonzero gap drifts beyond +/-2.0pt of its documented amount (new revisions landed: refresh the numbers from a fresh normalize run). New pins should only be added when a genuinely unhealable ESPN-side residual is observed.",
